# FakeWiki: no statics

Do not add `static` methods, `static` properties, or class-level constants to `FakeWiki`.

- Use instance methods and instance properties (including `private readonly` for configuration) so that behavior stays on the instance and is easier to test and override.
- If you need shared configuration, use an instance property (e.g. `private readonly BASE_URL = "..."`) and reference it as `this.BASE_URL`.
- If you need a concurrency helper or similar, implement it as an instance method and call it as `this.runWithConcurrency(...)` or `wiki.runWithConcurrency(...)` from hooks that receive a `FakeWiki` instance.
